From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm8650-lpass-lpi: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The LPI pin controller only has runtime PM ops and is a supplier of the
SoundWire controllers. When a SoundWire peripheral stays runtime-active the
controllers are force-suspended but keep their device links, so the pin
controller stays active with its LPASS votes through s2idle. Force the
runtime suspend across system sleep like the macros and the controller.

Needed on the Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 3 / Y700 2025 (TB321FU, SM8650).
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
index bc7889c99..e33d4360c 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pinctrl_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
